-- TuFFlevels / Routes/Alliance/NightElf.lua
--
-- ############################ READ THIS ############################
-- Mechanically converted, not hand-verified. Quest IDs and coordinates
-- came from a text-processing pass over a real, currently-maintained
-- guide (see Credits & License at the bottom of this file), not from
-- someone playing this route and confirming each step in-game.
--
-- Before trusting any of it, run:  /tuff verify
-- That checks every ID in this file against QuestieDB and reports
-- anything it can't find. Report problems found in-game back into this
-- file the normal way (see CONTRIBUTING.md) rather than discarding it.
-- ###################################################################
--
-- Night Elf starting zone (Shadowglen -> Teldrassil, converging straight into Darkshore) through
-- the full Alliance 1-60 leveling path (shared zones from ~level 21
-- onward: Stonetalon, Wetlands, Duskwood, Hillsbrad, Thousand Needles,
-- Stranglethorn Vale, Desolace, Swamp of Sorrows, Arathi, Dustwallow,
-- Badlands, Tanaris, Feralas, Searing Gorge, Blasted Lands, WPL, Felwood,
-- Azshara, UnGoro, Winterspring, Burning Steppes, Eastern Plaguelands,
-- Silithus).
--
-- Every step carries the same schema documented in the header of
-- Routes/Horde/Durotar.lua. Steps that only apply to one class carry a
-- `class` filter (e.g. class = "WARLOCK") the same way any hand-authored
-- route would - this route serves every class, not just one, the same
-- way Durotar.lua serves both Orc and Troll from one file.
--
-- SCOPE DECISIONS MADE DURING CONVERSION
--
-- The source guide is a branching graph (a finished zone sometimes offers
-- a player a choice of two different next zones), but TuFFlevels routes
-- are a single linear sequence. Where the source offered a choice, one
-- canonical path was picked (generally: whichever branch doesn't require
-- a specific non-default class, and when tied, the first-listed option) -
-- this means a real, valid alternate path through this level range exists
-- that this file doesn't include. Class-specific alternate leveling
-- METHODS (e.g. an AoE-grinding Mage path, a wholly different way to
-- level rather than a few different steps) and Season of Discovery
-- content were skipped entirely as out of scope for a Classic Era route.
-- A small number of steps (roughly 1 in 300) carry a note starting with
-- raw source syntax (e.g. a stray ".itemStat ...") where the source line
-- had no plain-language annotation to fall back to - still functional,
-- just not fully cleaned up prose.
--
-- Some steps use a numeric `map` (uiMapID) instead of a `zone` name where
-- the source guide gave a raw map ID directly rather than a zone name.
--
-- Two blocks of `forever = true` steps are original TuFFlevels additions,
-- not part of the RXPGuides conversion above: a Hall of Thanes chapter
-- (in "16-19 Darkshore", at this route's first Ironforge pass) and a
-- Ruins of Lordaeron chapter (spanning "27-29 Wetlands/Hillsbrad"). Both
-- are WoW Forever-only, provisional, and unverified in-game - see the
-- comment above each block for details.

